SCOPE OF THE PUBLIC DOMAIN DEDICATION

The dedication in UNLICENSE covers the original code and assets in this
repository.

It does not, and cannot, cover third-party material that this project merely
depends on or interoperates with — the Minecraft client, NeoForge, and any mod
whose blocks, items or APIs are referenced here. Those remain under their own
licences and none of their content is redistributed in this repository.

Compile-time dependencies are resolved from public mavens (Modrinth, NeoForged,
Architectury, FTB) at build time. No third-party jar is committed.

ARTIFACTS SOUND ASSETS

assets/fartbomb/sounds.json defines this mod's "big_fart" sound event in terms of
two sound files that belong to the Artifacts mod by ochotonida
(https://github.com/ochotonida/artifacts, MIT):

    artifacts:fart1
    artifacts:fart2

Those files are referenced by name and played from Artifacts' own assets at
runtime. Neither file, nor any derivative of either, is copied into or shipped by
this repository — the reference resolves only when Artifacts is installed, and the
sound event simply fails to load if it is not. Should a processed copy ever be
vendored here instead, MIT requires Artifacts' copyright notice and licence text to
travel with it, and this notice must be updated to say so.
